#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inputs {#inputs}"
msgstr "Input {#inputs}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every run is a single `fn.run(...)` call. Only the first three inputs in the table are required: `hamiltonian`, `t_steps`, and `aqc_segments`. Everything after them is optional and falls back to the default shown, so a minimal call is three arguments and the rest of the table is the functionality you can opt into. The Hamiltonian's `num_qubits` sets the chain length, so there is no separate size input.\n"
msgstr "Setiap larian ialah satu panggilan `fn.run(...)` tunggal. Hanya tiga input pertama dalam jadual diperlukan: `hamiltonian`, `t_steps`, dan `aqc_segments`. Semua selepasnya adalah pilihan dan kembali kepada lalai yang ditunjukkan, jadi panggilan minimum ialah tiga argumen dan selebihnya jadual ialah kefungsian tambahan yang boleh anda pilih. `num_qubits` bagi Hamiltonian menetapkan panjang rantai, jadi tiada input saiz berasingan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Input | Default | Description |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| `hamiltonian` | required | 1D nearest-neighbor Pauli Hamiltonian as a `SparsePauliOp`. Strings are Pauli operators, so there is no implicit factor of one half. |\n"
"| `t_steps` | required | Total Trotter steps. Evolves to `T = t_steps * dt` and reports every observable at each `t_k = k * dt`. |\n"
"| `aqc_segments` | required | Compression plan: a list of `{\"n_steps\": k, \"ansatz_steps\": m}`. `sum(n_steps)` steps are compressed; the rest run as plain Trotter. |\n"
"| `dt` | `0.2` | Physical time advanced by one Trotter step. |\n"
"| `initial_state` | `\\|0...0>` | A prepared `QuantumCircuit` to evolve. Bake any local kick into this circuit. |\n"
"| `observables` | per-site `Z` | Anything `EstimatorV2` accepts as its `observables` argument. One observable per output column. |\n"
"| `trotter_options` | 2nd-order Suzuki | `{\"method\": ..., \"synthesis_settings\": {...}}`. `reps` and `time` are owned by the workflow. |\n"
"| `aqc_options` | see description | `max_bond` (`32`), `cutoff` (`1e-8`), `autodiff_backend` (`\"jax\"`), `fidelity_target` (`None`), `optimizer_settings` (L-BFGS-B, `jac=True`, `maxiter=300`). |\n"
"| `estimator_options` | DD, twirling, TREX | `EstimatorV2.options`, passed through as-is. A supplied dictionary replaces the defaults wholesale rather than merging into them. |\n"
"| `transpiler_options` | `{\"optimization_level\": 3}` | `generate_preset_pass_manager` keyword arguments. `backend` and `target` are rejected, since the execution path owns them. |\n"
"| `backend` | `\"runtime\"` | `\"statevector\"`, `\"fake\"`, or `\"runtime\"`. |\n"
"| `backend_name` | least busy | IBM&reg; backend name for `runtime`, or a named fake backend. |\n"
"| `batches` | `1` | Split the circuits across N runtime jobs. One batch submits a single job and creates no session. |\n"
"| `parallel_sim` | `False` | Run the local simulator paths in parallel across all cores of the job's compute profile. No effect on `runtime`. |\n"
"| `return_circuits` | `False` | Return the logical AQC + Trotter circuits in the result alongside the observable series. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Input | Lalai | Keterangan |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| `hamiltonian` | diperlukan | Hamiltonian Pauli jiran terdekat 1D sebagai `SparsePauliOp`. String ialah operator Pauli, jadi tiada faktor tersirat satu perdua. |\n"
"| `t_steps` | diperlukan | Jumlah langkah Trotter. Berevolusi kepada `T = t_steps * dt` dan melaporkan setiap observable pada setiap `t_k = k * dt`. |\n"
"| `aqc_segments` | diperlukan | Pelan mampatan: senarai `{\"n_steps\": k, \"ansatz_steps\": m}`. Langkah `sum(n_steps)` dimampatkan; selebihnya dijalankan sebagai Trotter biasa. |\n"
"| `dt` | `0.2` | Masa fizikal yang dimajukan oleh satu langkah Trotter. |\n"
"| `initial_state` | `\\|0...0>` | `QuantumCircuit` yang disediakan untuk berevolusi. Bina sebarang tendangan tempatan ke dalam litar ini. |\n"
"| `observables` | `Z` per-tapak | Apa-apa yang diterima oleh `EstimatorV2` sebagai argumen `observables`-nya. Satu observable bagi setiap lajur output. |\n"
"| `trotter_options` | Suzuki peringkat ke-2 | `{\"method\": ..., \"synthesis_settings\": {...}}`. `reps` dan `time` dimiliki oleh aliran kerja. |\n"
"| `aqc_options` | lihat keterangan | `max_bond` (`32`), `cutoff` (`1e-8`), `autodiff_backend` (`\"jax\"`), `fidelity_target` (`None`), `optimizer_settings` (L-BFGS-B, `jac=True`, `maxiter=300`). |\n"
"| `estimator_options` | DD, twirling, TREX | `EstimatorV2.options`, dilalukan terus sebagaimana adanya. Kamus yang dibekalkan menggantikan lalai secara keseluruhan dan bukannya bercantum dengannya. |\n"
"| `transpiler_options` | `{\"optimization_level\": 3}` | Argumen kata kunci `generate_preset_pass_manager`. `backend` dan `target` ditolak, kerana laluan pelaksanaan memiliki keduanya. |\n"
"| `backend` | `\"runtime\"` | `\"statevector\"`, `\"fake\"`, atau `\"runtime\"`. |\n"
"| `backend_name` | paling tidak sibuk | Nama Backend IBM&reg; untuk `runtime`, atau Backend palsu yang dinamakan. |\n"
"| `batches` | `1` | Bahagikan litar merentasi N kerja runtime. Satu batch menghantar satu kerja tunggal dan tidak mencipta Session. |\n"
"| `parallel_sim` | `False` | Jalankan laluan simulator tempatan secara selari merentasi semua teras profil pengiraan kerja. Tiada kesan pada `runtime`. |\n"
"| `return_circuits` | `False` | Kembalikan litar logik AQC + Trotter dalam hasil bersama siri observable. |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execution backends {#execution-backends}"
msgstr "Backend pelaksanaan {#execution-backends}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All three paths share the same code and the same mitigation settings. They differ only in where the circuits run.\n"
msgstr "Ketiga-tiga laluan berkongsi kod yang sama dan tetapan mitigasi yang sama. Ia hanya berbeza pada tempat Circuit dijalankan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `backend` | What it is | Credentials | Notes |\n"
"|---|---|---|---|\n"
"| `\"statevector\"` | Exact `StatevectorEstimator` | Saved account only | The exact reference path. No QPU time. |\n"
"| `\"fake\"` | Noisy local simulation on a Qiskit fake backend | Saved account only | A faithful rehearsal of the mitigated `runtime` path. Needs `qiskit-aer`. Defaults to the 127-qubit `fake_sherbrooke`. |\n"
"| `\"runtime\"` (default) | The mitigated `EstimatorV2` against a real QPU | Saved account and an instance with QPU access | `backend_name` optional; omitting it selects the least busy device. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| `backend` | Apa itu | Bukti kelayakan | Nota |\n"
"|---|---|---|---|\n"
"| `\"statevector\"` | `StatevectorEstimator` yang tepat | Akaun tersimpan sahaja | Laluan rujukan yang tepat. Tiada masa QPU. |\n"
"| `\"fake\"` | Simulasi hingar tempatan pada Backend palsu Qiskit | Akaun tersimpan sahaja | Latihan yang setia bagi laluan `runtime` yang dimitigasi. Memerlukan `qiskit-aer`. Lalai kepada `fake_sherbrooke` 127-qubit. |\n"
"| `\"runtime\"` (lalai) | `EstimatorV2` yang dimitigasi terhadap QPU sebenar | Akaun tersimpan dan instance dengan akses QPU | `backend_name` pilihan; mengabaikannya memilih peranti paling tidak sibuk. |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both simulator paths still call the deployed workflow, so they need a saved account even though they use no QPU time. The two examples that follow run the same workload on `statevector` first, then on `runtime`.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua laluan simulator masih memanggil aliran kerja yang dideploy, jadi ia memerlukan akaun yang disimpan walaupun ia tidak menggunakan masa QPU. Dua contoh yang berikut menjalankan beban kerja yang sama pada `statevector` dahulu, kemudian pada `runtime`.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Output {#output}"
msgstr "Output {#output}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.result()` returns a plain dictionary:\n"
msgstr "`job.result()` mengembalikan kamus biasa:\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`aqc_fidelities` and `circuit_stats` are the two to read first: together they tell you whether the compression stayed faithful and whether it actually saved depth. On `runtime`, `resource_usage` reports the queue wait separately from the QPU time you are charged for. A rejected input fails fast as a structured `ServerlessError` (code `4615`).\n"
msgstr "`aqc_fidelities` dan `circuit_stats` ialah dua yang perlu dibaca dahulu: bersama-sama ia memberitahu anda sama ada mampatan kekal tepat dan sama ada ia benar-benar menjimatkan kedalaman. Pada `runtime`, `resource_usage` melaporkan masa menunggu giliran secara berasingan daripada masa QPU yang anda dikenakan bayaran. Input yang ditolak gagal dengan pantas sebagai `ServerlessError` berstruktur (kod `4615`).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulator example {#simulator-example}"
msgstr "Contoh simulator {#simulator-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the workflow on the exact `statevector` backend first. It spends no QPU time and validates the deployment end to end. The model here is an eight-qubit transverse-field Ising chain, and `observables` is omitted so the workflow measures the default per-site $Z$.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan aliran kerja pada Backend `statevector` yang tepat dahulu. Ia tidak menggunakan masa QPU dan mengesahkan deployment dari hujung ke hujung. Model di sini ialah rantai Ising medan-transversal lapan qubit, dan `observables` diabaikan supaya aliran kerja mengukur $Z$ per-tapak lalai.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The compression plan is the input worth understanding. Each segment `{\"n_steps\": k, \"ansatz_steps\": m}` compresses `k` consecutive Trotter steps into an ansatz built from an `m`-step Trotter target, and any steps beyond `sum(n_steps)` run as plain Trotter. Early, low-entanglement steps compress well into a shallow single-layer ansatz; later, more-entangled steps need a deeper one.\n"
msgstr "Pelan mampatan ialah input yang berbaloi untuk difahami. Setiap segmen `{\"n_steps\": k, \"ansatz_steps\": m}` memampatkan `k` langkah Trotter berturut-turut ke dalam ansatz yang dibina daripada sasaran Trotter `m`-langkah, dan mana-mana langkah melebihi `sum(n_steps)` dijalankan sebagai Trotter biasa. Langkah awal berkekusutan rendah dimampatkan dengan baik ke dalam ansatz satu lapisan yang cetek; langkah kemudian yang lebih berkekusutan memerlukan yang lebih dalam.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Follow the run and read the result {#follow-the-run-and-read-the-result}"
msgstr "Ikuti larian dan baca hasil {#follow-the-run-and-read-the-result}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`status()` reports both the coarse job lifecycle and the per-stage sub-status the workflow publishes as it runs. The same stages apply to the hardware run later in this guide:\n"
msgstr "`status()` melaporkan kedua-dua kitaran hayat kerja yang kasar dan sub-status setiap peringkat yang diterbitkan oleh aliran kerja semasa ia berjalan. Peringkat yang sama terpakai untuk larian perkakasan kemudian dalam panduan ini:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`QUEUED -> INITIALIZING -> RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE -> RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU -> RUNNING: EXECUTING_QPU -> RUNNING: POST_PROCESSING -> DONE`\n"
msgstr "`QUEUED -> INITIALIZING -> RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE -> RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU -> RUNNING: EXECUTING_QPU -> RUNNING: POST_PROCESSING -> DONE`\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| `status()` value | Stage |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE` | state preparation, Trotter build, AQC compression |\n"
"| `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU` | queued on the QPU (`runtime` backend only) |\n"
"| `RUNNING: EXECUTING_QPU` | circuits executing (local simulators mark this directly) |\n"
"| `RUNNING: POST_PROCESSING` | assembling the result dictionary |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Nilai `status()` | Peringkat |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE` | penyediaan keadaan, pembinaan Trotter, mampatan AQC |\n"
"| `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU` | dalam giliran pada QPU (Backend `runtime` sahaja) |\n"
"| `RUNNING: EXECUTING_QPU` | Circuit sedang dilaksanakan (simulator tempatan menandakan ini secara terus) |\n"
"| `RUNNING: POST_PROCESSING` | menyusun kamus hasil |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Terminal states are `DONE`, `ERROR`, and `CANCELED`. This `statevector` run has no QPU queue, so it skips `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. Use `job.logs()` at any point to see the per-stage logs, including the AQC fidelity reached at each step.\n"
msgstr "Keadaan terminal ialah `DONE`, `ERROR`, dan `CANCELED`. Larian `statevector` ini tiada giliran QPU, jadi ia melangkau `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. Guna `job.logs()` pada bila-bila masa untuk melihat log setiap peringkat, termasuk fideliti AQC yang dicapai pada setiap langkah.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hardware example {#hardware-example}"
msgstr "Contoh perkakasan {#hardware-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A workflow run with `backend=\"runtime\"` transpiles and executes on a real IBM Quantum processor, with the workflow's built-in error mitigation: dynamical decoupling (XY4), gate twirling, and twirled readout error extinction (TREX). `backend_name` selects the device; omit it and the workflow takes the least busy one.\n"
msgstr "Larian aliran kerja dengan `backend=\"runtime\"` melakukan transpile dan melaksanakan pada pemproses IBM Quantum sebenar, dengan mitigasi ralat terbina dalam aliran kerja: penyahgandingan dinamik (XY4), twirling gate, dan pemusnahan ralat pembacaan berpusing (TREX). `backend_name` memilih peranti; abaikan dan aliran kerja akan mengambil yang paling tidak sibuk.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nothing about the science code changes. What differs from the simulator example is the chain length, the number of Trotter steps, the compression plan, the backend, and the explicit mitigation settings covered in the following section.\n"
msgstr "Tiada apa-apa tentang kod sains yang berubah. Apa yang berbeza daripada contoh simulator ialah panjang rantai, bilangan langkah Trotter, pelan mampatan, Backend, dan tetapan mitigasi eksplisit yang dibincangkan dalam bahagian berikut.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sizing the job for the control hardware {#sizing-the-job-for-the-control-hardware}"
msgstr "Menetapkan saiz kerja untuk perkakasan kawalan {#sizing-the-job-for-the-control-hardware}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`estimator_options` is the input worth setting deliberately. Gate twirling builds `num_randomizations` separate randomized circuits for every PUB, and the whole job, every PUB with all of its randomizations, has to fit in the instruction memory of the QPU's classical control system. The workflow defaults to 1000 randomizations, so a 10-step evolution submits 11 PUBs of 1000 circuits each: roughly 11,000 circuit instances in a single job.\n"
msgstr "`estimator_options` ialah input yang berbaloi untuk ditetapkan secara sengaja. Twirling gate membina `num_randomizations` litar rawak berasingan untuk setiap PUB, dan keseluruhan kerja, setiap PUB dengan semua rawakannya, perlu muat dalam memori arahan sistem kawalan klasik QPU. Aliran kerja ini lalai kepada 1000 rawakan, jadi evolusi 10-langkah menghantar 11 PUB dengan 1000 litar setiap satu: lebih kurang 11,000 instance litar dalam satu kerja tunggal.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exceed what the control system holds and the job fails with [error 6073](https://ibm.biz/error_codes#6073). [Job limits](/guides/job-limits) gives the thresholds and how to count against them, the main one being 26.8 million control-system instructions per qubit, applied per job rather than per PUB. Dynamical decoupling adds gates that count toward it.\n"
msgstr "Melebihi apa yang dipegang oleh sistem kawalan dan kerja akan gagal dengan [ralat 6073](https://ibm.biz/error_codes#6073). [Had kerja](/guides/job-limits) memberikan ambang dan cara mengiranya, yang utama ialah 26.8 juta arahan sistem kawalan bagi setiap qubit, dikenakan per kerja bukannya per PUB. Penyahgandingan dinamik menambah Gate yang turut dikira dalam had tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two inputs control the size:\n"
msgstr "Dua input mengawal saiz:\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`estimator_options` sets the shot budget. Total shots is `num_randomizations * shots_per_randomization`, so you can trade randomizations against shots per randomization, keep the statistics, and still shrink the program. The following cell uses 100 randomizations at 200 shots each, which is 20,000 shots per observable and about a tenth of the circuit instances the defaults would submit. See [TwirlingOptions](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-twirling-options) and [Estimator options](/guides/estimator-options) for the full set of fields.\n"
msgstr "`estimator_options` menetapkan bajet shot. Jumlah shot ialah `num_randomizations * shots_per_randomization`, jadi anda boleh menukar ganti rawakan dengan shot per rawakan, kekalkan statistik, dan masih mengecilkan program. Sel berikut menggunakan 100 rawakan pada 200 shot setiap satu, iaitu 20,000 shot bagi setiap observable dan lebih kurang satu persepuluh daripada instance Circuit yang akan dihantar oleh lalai. Lihat [TwirlingOptions](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-twirling-options) dan [Pilihan Estimator](/guides/estimator-options) untuk set penuh medan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`batches` splits the PUBs across that many separate runtime jobs, which is the remedy error 6073 itself suggests and why the per-job framing matters. Setting `batches=4` sends roughly three PUBs per job instead of eleven at once, and the jobs go out together in one batch so the group queues once rather than each job queueing separately.\n"
msgstr "`batches` membahagikan PUB merentasi bilangan kerja runtime berasingan itu, yang merupakan penyelesaian yang dicadangkan oleh ralat 6073 itu sendiri dan sebab kerangka per kerja penting. Menetapkan `batches=4` menghantar lebih kurang tiga PUB per kerja bukannya sebelas sekali gus, dan kerja-kerja tersebut dihantar bersama-sama dalam satu batch supaya kumpulan itu beratur sekali bukannya setiap kerja beratur secara berasingan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remember that a supplied `estimator_options` replaces the workflow's defaults wholesale rather than merging into them, so dynamical decoupling and TREX are restated in the following cell to keep them switched on.\n"
msgstr "Ingat bahawa `estimator_options` yang dibekalkan menggantikan lalai aliran kerja secara keseluruhan dan bukannya bercantum dengannya, jadi penyahgandingan dinamik dan TREX dinyatakan semula dalam sel berikut untuk mengekalkannya dihidupkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Reconnecting to a long-running job\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Menyambung semula kepada kerja yang berjalan lama\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A hardware run is not quick, and most of the time is classical rather than on the QPU. The AQC compression runs inside the workflow before anything reaches the QPU, and the QPU queue is on top of that. You do not need to keep this notebook or kernel open while it runs.\n"
msgstr "Larian perkakasan tidak pantas, dan kebanyakan masa adalah klasik dan bukannya pada QPU. Mampatan AQC berjalan dalam aliran kerja sebelum apa-apa sampai ke QPU, dan giliran QPU adalah tambahan kepada itu. Anda tidak perlu memastikan notebook atau kernel ini terbuka semasa ia berjalan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Copy the job ID printed by the preceding cell and save it. The next three cells let you pick the run back up later:\n"
msgstr "Salin ID kerja yang dicetak oleh sel sebelumnya dan simpannya. Tiga sel berikutnya membolehkan anda menyambung semula larian kemudian:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reconnect, only needed in a new kernel session: re-run the [Authentication](#1-authentication) cell to recreate `client`, then rebuild the `job` handle from the ID you saved. Skip this cell if you are still in the session where you submitted, because the handle is already live.\n"
msgstr "Sambung semula, hanya diperlukan dalam sesi kernel baharu: jalankan semula sel [Pengesahan](#1-authentication) untuk mencipta semula `client`, kemudian bina semula pemegang `job` daripada ID yang anda simpan. Langkau sel ini jika anda masih dalam sesi di mana anda menghantar, kerana pemegang itu sudah aktif.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check status: re-run until it reports `DONE`.\n"
msgstr "Semak status: jalankan semula sehingga ia melaporkan `DONE`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fetch the result: run only once the status is `DONE`.\n"
msgstr "Dapatkan hasil: jalankan hanya setelah status ialah `DONE`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Paste your saved ID over the placeholder in the following reconnect cell.\n"
msgstr "Tampal ID yang anda simpan menggantikan pemegang tempat dalam sel sambung semula berikut.\n"

